%I A401549 #12 Nov 17 2026 13:55:55
%S A401549 24,12,48,20,8,12,16,2,120,4,24,12
%N A401549 Order of the symmetry group of the arrangement of n points on the 2-sphere that minimizes the covering radius, i.e., the maximum spherical distance of any point of the sphere from the nearest of the n points (covering of the sphere by n equal caps of minimal radius).
%C A401549 The order counts all isometries (rotations and reflections) mapping the point set onto itself.
%C A401549 Optimality of the covering has been proved for n = 4, 6, 12 (L. Fejes Tóth), n = 5, 7 (Schütte), n = 8 (Wimmer), n = 10, 14 (G. Fejes Tóth). For n = 9 Wimmer determined the combinatorial type of the solution. The remaining terms are conjectural; they correspond to the putatively optimal coverings of Hardin, Sloane and Smith and of Tarnai and Gáspár.
%C A401549 For n = 13 the optimal covering radius does not determine the configuration uniquely: one point is not involved in the critical (rigid) part of the covering and can be moved within an open region without changing the covering radius. In such cases the arrangement with the largest symmetry group is chosen. For n = 13 this gives a(13) = 4; a generic position of the free point gives symmetry order 1.
%C A401549 For n <= 20 all terms were independently confirmed by a numerical minimax optimization from random starts (Voronoi relaxation followed by sequential linear programming), see the Pfoertner links. The covering radii agree with the Hardin-Sloane-Smith table to all 7 given decimal places, and repeated runs converge to congruent configurations; n = 13 is the only case with a free point for n <= 20.
%C A401549 A conjectured continuation for n = 16..20 is 24, 4, 6, 2, 8.
%C A401549 For 4 <= n <= 20 this sequence differs from A081314 (maximal volume) only at n = 11.
%D A401549 Ernest Jucovič, Some coverings of a spherical surface with equal circles (in Slovakian), Matematicko-fyzikálny časopis, Slovensk. Akad. Vied. 10 (1960), 99-104.
